#{[17592186049950 :topic/next #edb/ref 17592186049590] [17592186049950 :topic/knowledge-points #edb/ref 17592186147516] [17592186049950 :topic/knowledge-points #edb/ref 17592186147517] [17592186049950 :topic/title "Solving Second-Order ODEs Using Laplace Transforms"] [17592186049950 :topic/math-academy-id 2540] [17592186049950 :topic/id #uuid "20a24bfd-943b-5aba-963d-d0ee1d8e479d"] [17592186147516 :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites #edb/ref 17592186048580] [17592186147516 :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites #edb/ref 17592186048605] [17592186147516 :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites #edb/ref 17592186050677] [17592186147516 :knowledge-point/questions #edb/ref 17592186148149] [17592186147516 :knowledge-point/questions #edb/ref 17592186148205] [17592186147516 :knowledge-point/questions #edb/ref 17592186237895] [17592186147516 :knowledge-point/questions #edb/ref 17592186351494] [17592186147516 :knowledge-point/questions #edb/ref 17592186351495] [17592186147516 :knowledge-point/questions #edb/ref 17592186351496] [17592186147516 :knowledge-point/questions #edb/ref 17592186377621] [17592186147516 :knowledge-point/questions #edb/ref 17592186377628] [17592186147516 :knowledge-point/questions #edb/ref 17592186377886] [17592186147516 :knowledge-point/questions #edb/ref 17592186593226] [17592186147516 :knowledge-point/questions #edb/ref 17592186593260] [17592186147516 :knowledge-point/questions #edb/ref 17592186593279] [17592186147516 :knowledge-point/questions #edb/ref 17592186596627] [17592186147516 :knowledge-point/questions #edb/ref 17592186596632] [17592186147516 :knowledge-point/questions #edb/ref 17592186607581] [17592186147517 :knowledge-point/questions #edb/ref 17592186147793] [17592186147517 :knowledge-point/questions #edb/ref 17592186147794] [17592186147517 :knowledge-point/questions #edb/ref 17592186318963] [17592186147517 :knowledge-point/questions #edb/ref 17592186318964] [17592186147517 :knowledge-point/questions #edb/ref 17592186318965] [17592186147517 :knowledge-point/questions #edb/ref 17592186318966] [17592186147517 :knowledge-point/questions #edb/ref 17592186377411] [17592186147517 :knowledge-point/questions #edb/ref 17592186377414] [17592186147517 :knowledge-point/questions #edb/ref 17592186593233] [17592186147517 :knowledge-point/questions #edb/ref 17592186593257] [17592186147517 :knowledge-point/questions #edb/ref 17592186596697] [17592186147517 :knowledge-point/questions #edb/ref 17592186607639] [17592186147516 :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Laplace Transform of a Second-Order ODE"] [17592186147517 :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Second-Order Initial Value Problem Using Laplace Transforms"] [17592186147516 :knowledge-point/canonical-example #edb/ref 17592186147364] [17592186147517 :knowledge-point/canonical-example #edb/ref 17592186147365] [17592186147516 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4487c2b9-b681-5e1d-a2d9-c3231afcf03d"] [17592186147517 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "30d5c275-af4a-5bdd-a97c-c937824d8e94"] [17592186147719 :activity/steps #edb/ref 17592186148435] [17592186147719 :activity/steps #edb/ref 17592186148436] [17592186147719 :activity/steps #edb/ref 17592186148437] [17592186147719 :activity/steps #edb/ref 17592186148438] [17592186147719 :activity/type #edb/ref 17592186045463] [17592186147719 :activity/title "Solving Second-Order ODEs Using Laplace Transforms"] [17592186147719 :activity/first-step #edb/ref 17592186148435] [17592186147719 :activity/scope #edb/ref 17592186049950] [17592186147719 :activity/id #uuid "c33fcd20-192a-525c-a003-08244d7958fe"] [17592186148435 :step/next #edb/ref 17592186148436] [17592186148436 :step/next #edb/ref 17592186148437] [17592186148437 :step/next #edb/ref 17592186148438] [17592186148435 :step/math-academy-id 604719] [17592186148436 :step/math-academy-id 604720] [17592186148437 :step/math-academy-id 604724] [17592186148438 :step/math-academy-id 604725] [17592186148435 :step/id #uuid "19d3669b-0462-5b59-8a2f-88a325af813e"] [17592186148436 :step/id #uuid "04d715c4-570a-53d3-be33-0a3fbcda94ed"] [17592186148437 :step/id #uuid "b201edef-c1ff-5f79-848c-4e3e546b3a32"] [17592186148438 :step/id #uuid "26d61a91-facd-5261-adc5-a1ee7c1d2edb"] [17592186148435 :step/content #edb/ref 17592186148757] [17592186148436 :step/content #edb/ref 17592186147516] [17592186148437 :step/content #edb/ref 17592186148758] [17592186148438 :step/content #edb/ref 17592186147517] [17592186148757 :tutorial/content "In this lesson, we will learn how to use Laplace transforms to solve second-order ODEs. As before, let's practice finding the Laplace transform of a second-order differential equation first.\n\nFor example, let's find the Laplace transform of $y(t)$ if \n\n$$\ny''  =  t, \\qquad y(0)=2, \\qquad y'(0)=3.\n$$\n\nFirst, we take the Laplace transform of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\mathcal{L}\\left\\{ y'' \\right\\} =  \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{ t \\right\\}\n$$\n\nNext, we simplify each side.\n\n- For the left-hand side, we use the formula for the Laplace transform of a second derivative. Letting $\\mathcal{L}\\left\\{ y \\right\\}=Y(s)$ and using the initial conditions $y(0)=2, \\, y'(0)=3,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{y}^{''}} & ={s}^{2}L{y}-sy(0)-{y}^{'}(0) \\\\  & ={s}^{2}Y(s)-sy(0)-{y}^{'}(0) \\\\  & ={s}^{2}Y(s)-2s-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the right-hand side, we use the following result from the table of Laplace transforms:\n\n$$\n\\mathcal{L} \\{  t  \\} = \\dfrac{1}{s^2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we can solve for $Y(s){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{y}^{''}} & =L{t} \\\\ {s}^{2}Y(s)-2s-3 & =\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}} \\\\ {s}^{2}Y(s) & =\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}}+3+2s \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{1}{{s}^{4}}+\\frac{3}{{s}^{2}}+\\frac{2}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Laplace transform of $y(t)$ is $Y(s) =  \\dfrac{1}{s^4} + \\dfrac{3}{s^2} + \\dfrac{2}{s}.$\n\nLet's see more examples."] [17592186148758 :tutorial/content "Now, let's see how to use Laplace transforms to solve second-order ODEs. There are two steps:\n\n- **Step 1:** Find the Laplace transform of the equation, and solve for $Y(s)$.\n\n- **Step 2:** Find the solution by taking the inverse Laplace transform.\n\nTo illustrate, let's continue solving the following differential equation:\n\n$$\ny''  =  t, \\quad y(0)=2, \\quad y'(0)=3\n$$\n\nEarlier, we found that the Laplace transform of $y(t)$ is\n\n$$\nY(s) =  \\dfrac{1}{s^4} + \\dfrac{3}{s^2} + \\dfrac{2}{s}.\n$$\n\nNow, we need to take the inverse Laplace transform. From the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{6}{{s}^{4}}} & ={t}^{3}, \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}}} & =t, \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, taking the inverse Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{Y(s)} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{{s}^{4}}+\\frac{3}{{s}^{2}}+\\frac{2}{s}} \\\\ y(t) & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{{s}^{4}}}+{L}^{-1}{\\frac{3}{{s}^{2}}}+{L}^{-1}{\\frac{2}{s}} \\\\ y(t) & =\\frac{1}{6}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{6}{{s}^{4}}}+3{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}}}+2{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\ y(t) & =\\frac{1}{6}{t}^{3}+3t+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the ODE is $y(t) = \\dfrac{1}{6} t^3 + 3 t + 2.$"] [17592186148757 :tutorial/math-academy-id 4113] [17592186148758 :tutorial/math-academy-id 4114] [17592186148757 :tutorial/id #uuid "d4b52997-ca96-5bc0-845a-b2943def6e25"] [17592186148758 :tutorial/id #uuid "1d2f1d1a-f65f-58b0-81e3-b67a89dcee71"] [17592186148757 :tutorial/title "Introduction"] [17592186148758 :tutorial/title "Using Laplace Transforms to Solve Second-Order Differential Equations"] [17592186147364 :question/math-academy-id "e-6663"] [17592186147365 :question/math-academy-id "e-6666"] [17592186147364 :question/problem "Find the Laplace transform $Y(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{y(t)\\right\\}$ for $s\\geq\\sqrt5$ if \n\n$$\ny'' - 5y = 4e^{-3t}, \\quad y(0)=2, \\quad y'(0)=-1.\n$$"] [17592186147365 :question/problem "Find $y(t)$ if the Laplace transform of the initial value problem\n\n$$\ny'' +  6y = 2\\sin {2t}, \\quad y(0) = 0, \\quad y'(0) = 2\n$$\n\nis given by\n\n$$\ns^2Y(s) - 2 +6 Y(s)  =  2\\left(\\dfrac{2}{s^2 + 4}\\right).\n$$"] [17592186147364 :question/id #uuid "8165df56-763a-5f36-9e21-9ed7b0e50190"] [17592186147365 :question/id #uuid "cfc54894-5add-5272-bf47-6495f5f4d288"] [17592186147364 :question/worked-solution "First, we take the Laplace transform of both sides and use the addition and scalar multiplication properties of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{y}^{″}-5y} & =L{4{e}^{-3t}} \\\\ L{{y}^{″}}-5L{y} & =4L{{e}^{-3t}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate $\\mathcal{L}\\left\\{y''\\right\\},$ we use the formula for the Laplace transform of a second derivative:\n\n$$\n\\mathcal{L}\\left\\{y''\\right\\}=s^2\\mathcal{L}\\left\\{y\\right\\}-sy(0)-y'(0)=s^2Y(s)-sy(0)-y'(0)\n$$\n\nTaking into account the given initial conditions, we get\n\n$$\n\\mathcal{L}\\left\\{y''\\right\\}=s^2Y(s)-2s+1.\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have the following result:\n\n$$\n\\mathcal{L}\\left\\{e^{-3t}\\right\\}=\\dfrac{1}{s+3}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can solve for $Y(s)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{y}^{″}}-5L{y} & =4L{{e}^{-3t}} \\\\ ({s}^{2}Y(s)-2s+1)-5Y(s) & =\\frac{4}{s+3} \\\\ ({s}^{2}-5)Y(s) & =\\frac{4}{s+3}+2s-1 \\\\ ({s}^{2}-5)Y(s) & =\\frac{4+(2s-1)(s+3)}{s+3} \\\\ ({s}^{2}-5)Y(s) & =\\frac{2{s}^{2}+5s+1}{s+3} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{2{s}^{2}+5s+1}{(s+3)({s}^{2}-5)}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186147365 :question/worked-solution "Using the transformed equation, we can solve for $Y(s)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{s}^{2}Y(s)-2+6Y(s) & =2(\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}+4}), \\\\ ({s}^{2}+6)Y(s) & =2+\\frac{4}{{s}^{2}+4} \\\\ ({s}^{2}+6)Y(s) & =\\frac{2{s}^{2}+12}{{s}^{2}+4} \\\\ ({s}^{2}+6)Y(s) & =\\frac{2({s}^{2}+6)}{{s}^{2}+4} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}+4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t}=\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}+4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the inverse Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{Y(s)} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}+4}} \\\\ y(t) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $y(t) =  \\sin {2t}$ is the solution of the original differential equation."]}
